      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for prescription ibuprofen in adults.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nWas this a typo or a mix-up with the daily total? Common options are:\n- **800 mg orally three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), for inflammatory or pain indications.\n- **400 mg orally every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), for general analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day** as the total, divided into the schedule you want.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
